MEM SIZE? 

R/S L2 BASIC
------------------------------
TRS-80 LEVEL II BASIC emulator
 Codeveloped with Claude, 2026
------------------------------
man pages available for all BASIC commands
"help meta" to display supported metacommands
READY
>NEW
READY
>10 REM T26 MODEL III CHR$(21)/CHR$(22) + LEVEL II CHR$(23) 32-COL MODE
>20 CLS
>30 PRINT CHR$(200);"X";
>40 A=PEEK(15368)
>50 REM CHR$(21): 192-255 BECOME CHARACTERS, NOT COMPRESSION
>60 PRINT CHR$(21);
>70 CLS
>80 PRINT CHR$(200);"X";
>90 B=PEEK(15360):C=PEEK(15361)
>100 REM CHR$(22) PICKS KATAKANA (DISPLAY ONLY); CHR$(21) BACK TO MODEL I
>110 PRINT CHR$(22);CHR$(21);
>120 CLS
>130 PRINT CHR$(196);"Y";
>140 D=PEEK(15364)
>150 REM CHR$(23): 32 CHARS/LINE -- EVEN BYTES, CURSOR STEPS 2
>160 CLS
>170 PRINT CHR$(23);"AB";
>180 E=PEEK(15360):F=PEEK(15361):G=PEEK(15362)
>190 P=POS(0)
>200 REM CLS RETURNS TO 64 CHARS/LINE
>210 CLS
>220 PRINT "AB";
>230 H=PEEK(15361)
>240 PRINT:PRINT "COMPRESS";A;"SPECIAL";B;C;"BACK";D
>250 PRINT "WIDE";E;F;G;P;"AFTERCLS";H
>260 END
>RUN
        XαX    YA B AB
COMPRESS 88 SPECIAL 200  88 BACK 89 
WIDE 65  32  66  2 AFTERCLS 66 
READY
>BYE
exit=0
